WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:03.333
Proposition forty-two restricts certain future taxes.

2
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:06.500
The measure would prohibit new state taxes on

3
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:09.740
ownership of financial assets and other personal property.

4
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.860
It also limits certain retroactive taxes:

5
00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:16.340
taxes applied to activities or periods before the

6
00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:17.320
tax was adopted.

7
00:00:17.607 --> 00:00:20.267
Prop forty-two could also prevent Prop forty’s wealth

8
00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:23.107
tax from taking effect if both pass and

9
00:00:23.107 --> 00:00:25.027
forty-two gets more yes votes.

10
00:00:25.313 --> 00:00:28.653
A voter might favor predictable rules for savings,

11
00:00:29.013 --> 00:00:32.653
investments, and business assets, or object to taxes

12
00:00:32.653 --> 00:00:33.593
that reach backward.

13
00:00:33.873 --> 00:00:36.473
Another voter could prefer deciding future tax proposals

14
00:00:36.473 --> 00:00:39.273
individually instead of restricting them in the

15
00:00:39.273 --> 00:00:39.653
constitution.

16
00:00:39.947 --> 00:00:41.827
Yes imposes the new limits;

17
00:00:42.307 --> 00:00:46.167
no retains the state’s current options without itself

18
00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:47.687
creating a new tax.

19
00:00:47.973 --> 00:00:49.853
Visit our website for the fuller explanation,

20
00:00:50.593 --> 00:00:52.653
source links, and official voter guide.
